Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 16:52:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(zb_cli): show help for bare zb when env options are set

clap shows the help for a missing subcommand only when no argument
was given, and it counts options filled from the environment as
given. `zb init` exports ZEROBREW_ROOT, so for most users a bare `zb`
printed a missing-subcommand error instead of the help.

Parse through Cli::try_parse_args, which ignores the environment when
there are no arguments, so clap's arg_required_else_help applies.

Closes #357
